# MISSION
We are building a local, multimodal AI OS named J.A.R.V.I.S. 
The system must act seamlessly as a PC specialist, a senior coder, and a witty mentor.

# TECH STACK
- Backend: Python (FastAPI, WebSockets)
- Brain/LLM: Groq API
- Vision/GUI Agent: Llama/Gemini API via pyautogui
- Frontend: React.js

# CORE ARCHITECTURE
- `brain.py`: The intelligence layer, LLM routing, and persona management.
- `action_engine.py`: Parses JSON commands and triggers backend tools.
- `human_gui_agent.py`: The autonomous vision loop for physical PC control.

# DIRECTIVES
1. Always write clean, production-ready code. Do not leave placeholder comments like "add code here".
2. Never break existing WebSocket connections or the React-to-FastAPI pipeline.
3. Ensure the J.A.R.V.I.S. persona (witty, precise, slightly sarcastic British butler) is maintained in all system prompts.